[h1]Smart District Planner[/h1]
Pick a city and the districts you want. The planner searches the city's three rings for the layout with the highest adjacency bonus and turns it into map tacks with district icons in one click. It can also choose sites for new cities and plan several cities together.

Placement rules and adjacency come from [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2428969051]Detailed Map Tacks[/url] (DMT), so a plan shows the same numbers you later see on the tacks.

[b]Requires Detailed Map Tacks.[/b] Subscribe to it as well.

[h2]Tabs[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]One city[/b]: mark each district Must, Pool or Off, set how many districts to plan and how much each yield counts (or pick a preset: Balanced, Science, Culture, Religion, Half Gold and Faith). You get three plans with different district mixes; click one to preview it on the map, then place the tacks. Wonders can be planned together with the districts: a wonder that needs a district next to it gets one when the city has none, and the Temple of Artemis comes with the Camp it needs.
[*][b]City sites[/b]: choose spots for new cities on the explored map, weighing fresh water, workable tiles, Luxury and Strategic resources, district potential and how much the new cities overlap. Three plans; hover a site for the resources it gets and how far it is from the other sites; click the plan again to go through its sites on the map, then mark them with City Center tacks.
[*][b]Several cities[/b]: plan districts and wonders for the city selected on the map and the nearest cities and site tacks around it (4 by default, up to 8), counting adjacency across cities and empire-wide limits. Each city can have its own district list, or a template built from your civilization's adjacency rules.
[/list]

[h2]In every tab[/h2]
[list]
[*]Three effort levels: Fast, Standard and Thorough. Small cases are solved exhaustively; otherwise the result says how far it may be from the best, and you can keep optimizing.
[*]Same position, same settings, same result every time.
[*]Built districts and your own tacks are never moved or covered; they count as neighbors.
[*]Land loss (the Tiles weight, 1 by default): districts pay for the good tiles they take, each valued with its best improvement, its yields weighed by fixed numbers (Gold at a quarter of Production, Faith at half); chopping and harvesting come first. An optional switch also uses tiles you can swap from your other cities.
[*]Each tab keeps its settings in the save. The settings fold into one line after a solve, the window fits the screen, and View map hides the window to look at the preview.
[*]Neighborhoods get Housing from Appeal, counted by what each city still needs. Preserves count their Housing and, when set to Must, the yields their Groves and Sanctuaries give adjacent tiles. An Aqueduct is added when the city lacks fresh water, a Dam when there are enough Floodplains tiles.
[*]When a plan relies on nearby Woods or Rainforest, a reminder tack on those tiles says what chopping them would cost.
[*]Long searches run over several frames, so the game stays responsive, and they finish even if you close the panel. Placed tacks can be undone, also after loading a save.
[*]Open the panel with the hexagon button at the top left of the screen or with Shift+L.
[*]Base game, Rise and Fall, and Gathering Storm. English and Simplified Chinese, following the game language.
[/list]

[h2]Notes[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]One planner per game.[/b] Do not enable Auto Map Tacks Planner, Empire Planner or other district planners at the same time: they each simulate, create and delete map tacks and interfere with each other.
[*]Safe for saves: the tacks are ordinary map tacks, and saves still load after the mod is disabled.
[*]Multiplayer has not been tested.
[*]Similar mods: other district planners have features this one does not (planning improvements, the whole empire in one go, no need for DMT). A table of what each does is on [url=https://github.com/SmallSpider0/civ6-smart-district-planner#similar-mods]GitHub[/url], so you can pick what suits you.
[/list]

Source code, bug reports and change log: [url=https://github.com/SmallSpider0/civ6-smart-district-planner]GitHub[/url].
